```
# ============================================================================
# Detection: Impossible Travel Between Successive Logins
# Detection ID: DE-IA-003
# MITRE ATT&CK: T1078 - Valid Accounts
# Data Source: Azure AD / Okta Sign-In Logs
# Severity: High
# ============================================================================

index=auth sourcetype IN ("azure:aad:signin","okta:sso")
| eval account=coalesce(UserPrincipalName, actor.alternateId)
| sort 0 account, _time
| streamstats current=f last(_time) as prev_time last(src_lat) as prev_lat last(src_lon) as prev_lon last(city) as prev_city by account
| eval time_delta_hrs=round((_time-prev_time)/3600,2)
| eval distance_km=round(acos(
    sin(pi()*src_lat/180)*sin(pi()*prev_lat/180) +
    cos(pi()*src_lat/180)*cos(pi()*prev_lat/180)*cos(pi()*prev_lon/180 - pi()*src_lon/180)
  )*6371,1)
| eval implied_speed_kmh=round(distance_km/time_delta_hrs,1)
| where implied_speed_kmh>900 AND time_delta_hrs>0 AND distance_km>500
| table _time, account, prev_city, city, distance_km, time_delta_hrs, implied_speed_kmh
```

## Detection Logic
Calculates great-circle distance between geolocated successive logins for the same account and derives an implied travel speed. Speeds exceeding commercial aircraft cruise speed (~900 km/h) indicate credential compromise rather than legitimate travel.

## False Positive Considerations
VPN/proxy exit-node hopping and corporate mobile-device-management geolocation errors are the dominant false-positive source — cross-reference with known corporate VPN egress IP ranges lookup.

## Tuning Notes
Lower the threshold cautiously; frequent travelers and VPN split-tunnel users need a documented exception process rather than blanket suppression.
